# rule 24: whether a file is the one the editor saw earlier is judged in
# we_seen.c, by wpe_seen_judge, never by an inode number kept from an earlier
# moment (a file system gives a number back after its file is gone).
# Clause a (r24a) is st_ino and st_dev, b (r24b) a member of a WpeSeen read
# outside we_seen.c, c (r24c) statx and the birth-time names, d (r24d) the
# folder numbers kept by hand and the three-argument identity question, e
# (r24e) a test that asserts "another inode" with nothing held, f (r24f) the
# file the user was shown passed to the mode owner as anything but a WpeSeen
# called shown, g (r24g) a call of the bridge wpe_seen_into_stat.  Each pass
# deletes the rows of the sites it moves onto the owner: N2 the write owner and
# the assistant's look, N3 the mode owner, N4 the assistant's checkpoint and
# window lookup, N5 the two-look sites and the tests.
# Two sites compare the .dev and .ino members of an old record and spell no
# st_ino, so clause a cannot list them:
#  - the assistant's remembered Yes (we_ai_ui.c, the ai_linked_yes record and
#    ai_linked_yes_recalls and _remember).  It belongs to N4, but it stops
#    compiling in N2, when WpeWriteExpect loses its dev and ino members, so N2
#    must keep it building and N4 moves it onto a WpeSeen.
#  - the Attributes dialog (we_fl_unix.c, WpeFileDirAttributes).  It passes a
#    struct stat as the shown record through wpe_fileop_chmod_shown into
#    wpe_write_set_perm_seen, and the build accepts that incompatible pointer,
#    so nothing breaks when the type changes.  Clause f lists it (r24f rows
#    below); N3 must move it by hand onto a WpeSeen called shown.
# N3: the mode owner
we_write.c|r24g:wpe_write_add_perm|1|N3|site 8: Ctrl-F9 hands the window's record to the mode owner as a number
we_write.c|r24a:write_mode_same_file|4|N3|site 11: the descriptor is the file lstat saw
we_write.c|r24a:write_mode_shown_kind|2|N3|site 7: a link took the name, or another file
we_write.c|r24a:wpe_write_name_seen|2|N3|site 7: the name's record
we_write.c|r24f:wpe_write_set_perm_seen|1|N3|the definition takes the shown record as a struct stat
we_write.h|r24f:wpe_write_set_perm_seen|1|N3|the prototype takes the shown record as a struct stat
we_fileop.c|r24f:wpe_fileop_chmod_shown|1|N3|the definition takes the shown record as a struct stat
we_fileop.h|r24f:wpe_fileop_chmod_shown|1|N3|the prototype takes the shown record as a struct stat
we_fl_unix.c|r24f:WpeFileDirAttributes|1|N3|the Attributes dialog passes its struct stat as the shown record
# N4: the assistant
we_ai_ws.c|r24a:ws_record_root|2|N4|site 9: the workspace folder's number kept by hand
we_ai_ws.c|r24d:ws_record_root|2|N4|site 9: ck_rdev and ck_rino
we_ai_ws.c|r24a:ws_root_unchanged|2|N4|site 9: the revert trusts the folder by its number
we_ai_ws.c|r24d:ws_root_unchanged|2|N4|site 9: ck_rdev and ck_rino
we_ai_ws.c|r24d:ck_clear|2|N4|site 9: ck_rdev and ck_rino reset
we_ai_ws.c|r24d:wpe_ai_read_scope_file|2|N4|the file-scope declarations of ck_rdev and ck_rino, counted under the function above them
